    "notes": "Three sessions in May-June 1962 at Sound Makers Studio, NYC. Companion album to Moon Beams (the ballad selections). Wikipedia lists tracks 1,6 on 1962-05-17; 5,7,9 on 1962-05-29; 2-3,8 on 1962-06-05. Alternate take track 4 (In Your Own Sweet Way alt.) is from the same June 5 session. Apple Music OJC edition tracks 9-11 add alt. takes; only track 4 (the original bonus track) is included here."
  },
  "ballot": {
    "tier": "contested",
    "priority": "strong",
    "case_for": "This is a key document of Evans's second major trio: the post-LaFaro partnership with Chuck Israels and Paul Motian, recorded in three May-June 1962 sessions. Its buoyant, uptempo program gives the listener a complementary view of Evans beyond the better-known balladic and LaFaro-era records, while the Earl Zindars title tune became an enduring Evans staple.",
    "case_against": "The album is a tempo-selected companion to Moon Beams rather than an entirely coherent new statement, and its studio material lacks the defining historical force of Sunday at the Village Vanguard, Waltz for Debby, Portrait in Jazz, or Explorations.",
    "recommendation": "The council proposes that John give this a strong but non-core inclusion consideration.",
